# local tooling / editor. `.claude/` is ignored except what every worktree needs: the
# three files that carry the worktree-per-change rule, the launch config the preview
# starts the static server from, and the four directories Claude Code reads project
# skills, subagents, commands and scripts from. A worktree only gets a file if git puts
# it there, so anything ignored here is missing from the tree every change is made in —
# which is why the config directories have to be listed even while they are empty. See
# docs/agents/claude-code-and-opus-5.md.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/worktree-per-change.json
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/launch.json
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/scripts/
.openai/
.agents/
.codex/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log

# the build's inputs and outputs. dist/ is what the deployment serves and is
# assembled from scratch on every build — Astro's output plus the static tree
# copied in beside it — so a committed copy could only ever be stale. .astro/ is
# the types Astro generates for `astro check` and is regenerated the same way.
node_modules/
.vercel/
dist/
.astro/

# The author's own denylist of unpublishable terms — the clients, colleagues and
# hostnames a Section's words may not contain. It is NOT committed, and that is
# the point: a list of the names in a public repository is the leak the Check
# exists to prevent. scripts/checks/lib/denylist.mjs holds the shapes, which are
# the half that is safe to publish.
scripts/checks/lib/denylist.local.txt

# where check-capture-contract.py used to stage the profile repo's capture script
# and the screenshots it took. #148 deleted that script — the capture is asked
# for rather than replayed here, and docs/agents/external-capture.md says why —
# but the rule stays for a while: a tree that ran it before pulling this has a
# directory of run output in it, and an ignore that outlives its writer costs
# nothing while an accidentally committed vendored copy of another repo's script
# costs a rewrite.
#
# DELETE THIS RULE once no checkout has the directory. `ls -d
# design/tools/.capture-contract` across the main checkout and every worktree is
# the whole test; the main checkout had 20K of it on 2026-08-23. Nothing writes
# it any more, so the day it is gone everywhere it is gone for good.
design/tools/.capture-contract/

# the confirmed photographs baked down to a handful of blocks each, by
# design/censor/mosaic.py, for design/censor/capture-origin.mjs to serve in the
# vault's place while the clip is recorded. Derivatives of a real personal
# library — the same reason photos/ below is ignored — and what ships is the
# finished clip in portfolio/video/, which IS committed. Rebuild them with one
# command; capture-origin.mjs refuses to serve against a stale bake.
design/censor/mosaic/

# stills the Frame's material is judged over, captured through the censored
# origin above by design/frame-glass/shoot.mjs. Obscured pixels rather than raw
# ones, and STILL not committed: what ships is the clip in portfolio/video/, and
# a still of a real library kept in the tree to make a colour choice checkable is
# exactly what the origin exists to avoid. Rebuild with one command.
design/frame-glass/local/

# where `record` writes when it is handed design/record as its workspace. The
# Project and its Action are committed — they are the settings the clip was made
# with — and the Runs are not: ten of them per Action, each carrying the same
# photographs the clip does, on this machine only. record's own repository
# ignores its runs/ and published/ for the same reasons.
design/record/runs/
design/record/published/

# python bytecode. Most of design/ is Python generators — eighteen of them — and
# every directory holding one grows a __pycache__ as soon as anything imports it,
# which `python -m compileall design/` alone is enough to do in eight of them. So
# no list here: unanchored, matching at every depth, deliberately.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# full-resolution photo originals (~250MB) — the site uses the optimised copies
# in img/. Kept local to keep the repo lean and Vercel deploys fast. Regenerate
# img/ from these with the Pillow step in README.md.
photos/

# camera raws, wherever they are dropped. Same reasoning as photos/ — a single
# RW2 off the GX80 is ~19MB — but by extension, because the one the corner plate
# is built from is handed to design/plate/build-plate.py by path and so tends to
# sit wherever it was unpacked rather than under photos/.
*.rw2

# ...and the same for a cut-out plate source, which is a 20MB RGBA PNG and gets
# dropped in the same place — three of them, one per corner picture, under opaque
# content-hash filenames. They are handed to design/plate/build-plate.py by path,
# and design/plate/sources/README.md records which hash feeds which picture,
# because nothing in the filename does.
design/plate/sources/*

# the Texturelabs plates the textures are baked from, two of them at 9MB and
# 12MB. What ships is portfolio/img/tex/, which IS committed. There is a licence
# reason as well as a size one: texturelabs.org asks that the source files not be
# redistributed as textures, and a baked, cut-down, blended derivative is a
# different thing from the original asset. Attribution is in
# portfolio/img/tex/README.md, and the script is design/effects/build-textures.py.
design/effects/sources/*

# EVERY ONE OF THESE USED TO BE A ROOT-ANCHORED RULE — `/*.png`,
# `/Texturelabs_*.jpg`, `/Gemini_Generated_Image_*.jpg` — because each generator
# took its input "from the repo root". That put 110MB of unrelated pictures in the
# one directory a reader looks at first, told them nothing about which script
# wanted which file, and — the reason this changed rather than merely the reason
# it is tidier — made it impossible to see at a glance whether one of them was
# TRACKED. A per-file root ignore is a rule about a name; a directory ignore is a
# rule about a place, and a place can be listed. An ignored input now lives in a
# `sources/` directory beside the ONE generator that reads it, and these three
# lines are the safety net for the old habit:
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg

# ...and the 2x2 lay-up build-textures.py writes beside the paper tile so its
# seams can be looked at rather than taken on trust. A diagnostic, rebuilt on
# every run, and nothing serves it.
portfolio/img/tex/paper-seam-proof.png

# the Variant sheet, and the renders it is assembled from. design/tools/
# render-variants.mjs wipes and rewrites this directory on every run, and what it
# holds is a picture of the source it was run against — so a committed copy could
# only ever be a picture of a Variant that has since been rewritten, captioned
# with the declarations it used to have. `pnpm variants` is a minute.
design/sheets/

# design/tools/render-stages.mjs's own output — the two stages of the Eater Map's
# Exploded View side by side (#181). Beside design/sheets/ rather than under it,
# because the Variant sheet wipes its whole directory on every run.
design/stages/

# secrets — never commit
.env
.env.*

# the maps design/plinth/build-portoro-maps.py writes from the AI-generated Nero
# Portoro plate. Same rule as the Texturelabs plates above: sources and
# intermediates stay out, the bake ships. The plate ITSELF is covered by the
# design/plinth/sources/ rule below — it used to have a /Gemini_Generated_Image_*
# line of its own at the root, and there were two copies of it, one at each
# place. Unlike the Texturelabs plates there is no upstream to re-fetch this one
# from - see docs/agents/plinth-marble.md.
design/plinth/maps/

# ...and where design/plinth/plinth-studio.py keeps the photographs dropped on
# it. Same rule again, and worth saying out loud because this is the one that
# arrives by drag-and-drop rather than by being put somewhere deliberately: a
# stone's ENTRY and PLATE are committed and the image it was cut from is not, so
# a stone can be looked at in a fresh checkout and can only be RE-BAKED in a tree
# that still has this directory. Keep anything you care about elsewhere too.
design/plinth/sources/

# the design renders and reference photographs a composition was MEASURED off
# rather than baked from — the Projects Panel's own render is the one that
# matters, and design/reference/README.md is where the numbers in the `.panel`
# block point. Ignored for a reason that is not size: it is a screenshot of the
# real photo grid and carries uncensored pictures of real people, which is the
# rule photos/ above is under. The README is committed and the pictures are not,
# so a fresh checkout gets the reason without the exposure.
design/reference/*
!design/reference/README.md

# ...and the same negation for the source directories above, so the note saying
# which file is which survives a clone that has none of them.
!design/plate/sources/README.md
!design/effects/sources/README.md

# per-candidate plinth shots from render.mjs --stones. 1.4MB each and
# regenerable in a minute; what is committed is the contact sheet built from
# them, design/shots/plinth-stones.jpg.
design/shots/*__stone-*.png